  "_comment": "Pszczyna, Poland: a closed loop of real streets and the real alleys of the Park Zamkowy (castle park), from OpenStreetMap. The park alleys are footways and paths, opened as a 7 m stage road for this one track (the user asked for a lap through the park; every other street stage keeps to public roads). The start line and the pit lane (on the park side) are on ul. Katowicka heading south below Rondo św. Jadwigi Śląskiej. The lap: south down ul. Katowicka over the Pszczynka, right at ul. Dworcowa into the cobbled ul. Piastowska, west across the Rynek and out past Brama Wybrańców to ul. Wojska Polskiego beside Pszczyna Castle, right (north) onto ul. Żorska over the Pszczynka past the Pokazowa Zagroda Żubrów (the wisent show enclosure, OSM way 977929799, its herd stands in the enclosure's east corner, 'extra_landmarks'), right through the park's west gate onto the asphalt alley along the big pond's north shore, south-east to a hairpin on the lawn north of the castle, north across the bridges between the two central ponds, the sett alley north-west, round the park's western lobe and out onto ul. Chopina by Dwór Ludwikówka, east along Chopina past the Staw Chuchółka pond, right at Rondo św. Jadwigi Śląskiej and back down ul. Katowicka. Piastowska and the Rynek's east side are tagged access=no / motor_vehicle=no (pedestrianised old town); the direction driven follows every one-way. The route ways and nodes were picked on the OSM footway graph (park alleys between waypoints), so the route lists its nodes. See tools/build_street_tracks.py for the keys.",
